{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1530234-book-of-seemings-preview-q-a-coming-next-week","id":1530234,"title":"Book of Seemings preview/Q&A (coming next week!)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-07T18:33:04-08:00","id":1530234,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Book of Seemings preview/Q&A (coming next week!)","content":"EDIT: Get it here:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/470934/Book-of-Seemings?affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Book of Seemings</b></a><br /> <br /> Discount/previous buyer bundles:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/470935/Lost-and-Resurrected-BUNDLE?affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Book of Seemings + Bloodlines: The Resurrected</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/470936/Lost-in-Rome-BUNDLE?affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Book of Seemings + Requiem for Rome 2E</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/470937/Lost-in-Time-BUNDLE?affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Book of Seemings + Bloodlines: The Ageless</b></a><br /> <br /> <i><b><u>NMD PATREON: </u></b></i><a href=\"http://patreon.com/NoneMoreDarkPublishing\" target=\"_blank\"><u><b><i>patreon.com/NoneMoreDarkPublishing</i></b></u></a><br /> <hr /><br /> Hello, folks. Time to return to Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Some of you who follow the doings of None More Dark Publishing might know that we have a book for <b>Changeling: The Lost Second Edition</b> in the works: the <b>Book of Seemings</b>. Well, I\u2019m here to tell you it\u2019s coming next week as a little Valentine\u2019s Day present to all you CofD fans (i.e., Wednesday, February 14th). At 12 PST, that\u2019ll be dropping on DTRPG and the Storytellers Vault.<br /> <br /> If you don\u2019t know who/what NMD is, we\u2019re a collective of RPG authors and artists who\u2019ve spent the last two years creating supplements for <b>Vampire: The Requiem Second Edition</b>. Because the current IP owner has stopped approving new official releases for the Chronicles of Darkness (to the best of my knowledge; I have no other information in that regard beyond what everyone else has seen), we\u2019ve been trying to carry the torch, at least with <b>Vampire</b>, and now <b>Changeling </b>(though I believe there\u2019s one more official <b>Lost </b>book in the works regarding the Hedge?)<br /> <br /> So, what\u2019s in this book? Let me quote the back cover. <b>Book of Seemings </b>includes:<ul><li>A complete player and Storyteller\u2019s guide to the six seemings.</li> <li>Twelve kiths and twelve entitlements embodying each seeming\u2019s beautiful madness.</li> <li>Six seeming-specific systems to add to your chronicles, including sumptuous Feasts, vast Liebraries, and deadly Wild Runs.</li> <li>The Forgotten, almost-changelings who lost their souls to the Thorns and fill the void with living flesh.</li> <li>New Archetypes, frailties, and Merits, as well as 240 seeming benefits not included in the Changeling rulebook.</li> </ul>I\u2019ll get into the specifics more in the coming week, but for now, I\u2019ll leave you with a short preview of two of the kiths we\u2019re including.<br /> <br /> ALSO, NMD is going to be setting up a Patreon to go along with this release (assuming we get our asses in gear in time). So, if you'd like to support us in other ways than just buying our books, we'll have more about that soon.<br /> <br /> <b>New Kiths on the Block</b><br /> <br /> Most of the following kiths are drawn from <b>Changeling: The Lost First Edition</b>, converted here to fit with the current system/setting. As such, they\u2019ve retained their associated seemings from that version of the game: While the Gentry can shape a Beast into a Drudge, making her a farm animal continually sold for magic beans, the majority of Drudges are Wizened. Players and Storytellers shouldn\u2019t feel limited to always using these kiths with the seemings listed here, but consider what factors might lead to any outliers.<br /> <br /> <b>Dancer (Fairest)</b><br /> <br /> <i>Only through movement are we truly alive \u2014 truly in control.</i><br /> <br /> The magnetism of Dancers is due not to how they look, but how they move. The Gentry steal away the lithest, the quickest, or the most flexible, or just those with the best rhythm. Then, the Dancers\u2019 bodies are stretched, carved, or perfected with clockwork timing \u2014 whatever\u2019s necessary to push their coordination beyond the scope of human limitations. Once their precision and swiftness are unparalleled, they\u2019re set to their singular purpose. They make it look effortless \u2014 regardless of the agonies of fulfilling their task.<br /> <br /> Some seduce as lithesome assassins, drawing their prey in with hypnotic movements like cobras preparing to strike. Others dance mad jigs for weeks without rest until the Gentry finally let the music box wind down to silence. A few leap over the very moon and pirouette among the firmament so they can gather up the stardust for their masters to lay into the eyes of sleeping babes. Their physicality is spellbinding \u2014 literally.<br /> <br /> The trouble with perfection, though, is there\u2019s no further pinnacle to reach. Dancers become so specialized they can\u2019t bend to ever-changing Faerie whims. Once they realize their full potential, they rebel. They use their Fae-given grace to break free. Then, not even the wind can catch them.<br /> <br /> Out of the Hedge, many Dancers are faced with an equally fascinated audience among the Lost. Most fall back on their grace because it\u2019s become all they can do, but now they get to choose for whom they dance and when they stop. That sort of bodily autonomy is the most freeing of all.<br /> <br /> <b>Kith Blessing</b><br /> <br /> When a Dancer uses Expression to physically perform for an audience (through dance, martial arts, mime, gymnastics, etc.), achieving three successes counts as an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> <i>Gossamer Grace: </i>[REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Drudge (Wizened)</b><br /> <br /> <i>Always the quiet ones you should watch out for\u2026</i><br /> <br /> Humans often say the best servant is the one you don\u2019t even know is there. The Gentry agree, and many of them train their changeling slaves to stay out of sight and mind. Drudges are discreet, keep their heads down, and avoid attracting attention as they flit from room to room, keeping everything in a state of perfection.<br /> <br /> Drudges escape Arcadia by falling beneath their Keeper\u2019s notice and slipping out the backdoor so quietly no one realizes they\u2019re gone until weeks \u2014 or even years \u2014 later. Some rig elaborate contraptions to fake their household chores and buy themselves just enough time to escape, while others pawn their duties off onto goblins without telling anyone, so all their overseer sees is that the job gets done as usual.<br /> <br /> The Winter Court makes a concerted effort to recruit Drudges; their naturally unassuming demeanor makes them excellent spies for the Silent Arrows. In freeholds where this is common, the kith may be treated with suspicion by other courtiers, but Drudges shrug it off and get back to work. Every court needs someone who knows how to run a home, and many relish the opportunity to maintain a base of operations or work with newly escaped Lost settling back into the mortal world.<br /> <br /> <b>Kith Blessing</b><br /> <br /> When a Drudge uses Stealth in a domestic setting, achieving three successes counts as an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> <i>A Day\u2019s Work:</i> [REDACTED]\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 02-14-2024, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T08:58:52-08:00","id":1530280,"title":"","content":"Elementals burn<br /> Beasts howl<br /> Fairest sing<br /> And Darklings prowl<br /> <br /> Wizened tinker<br /> And Ogres lurch<br /> The Forgotten hunger<br /> While the Huntsmen search<br /> <br /> Boil boil, toil and trouble<br /> Fire burn and cauldron bubble<br /> By the pricking of my thumbs<br /> Something LOST this way comes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 02-08-2024, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T12:51:49-08:00","id":1530309,"title":"","content":"So, I promised the <b>Scarecrow Minister</b>, one of two Darkling entitlements, but first, a bit of context.<br /> <br /> Entitlements aren't normally tied to seemings. This isn't true of First or Second Edition. However, we wanted to provide character options tuned to each seeming. So, we suggest that these entitlements are <i>mostly </i>borne by members of particular seemings (boy I wish there were an alternate word for seeming, because seeming has lost all meaning in the last 6 months). We don't lock other...fae legacies?...out of these entitlements, but we suggest that such a case would be the exception to the rule. This is explained more in the introduction of the entitlement chapter.<br /> <br /> As for the Minister, this is probably the entitlement you think of when you think of changeling entitlements. Like, that's the one we all know and love. The Minister is certainly <i>my </i>problematic fave.<br /> <br /> The Scarecrow Ministry here isn't too different from the original version, albeit he's just one Darkling now. One thing I loved about the way <b>Oak, Ash, and Thorn </b>handled entitlements was making each one a unique title, and that fit the Minister <i>really </i>well (who actually gets a few shout outs in <b>OAT</b>).<br /> <br /> I don't have much to add here in terms of development, because the developer wrote this one, and I didn't really change anything! So, without further ado, here's the Scarecrow Minister. Tomorrow, let's check out another new system: Ogre <b>Feasts</b>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Scarecrow Minister</b><br /> <br /> <i>It\u2019s okay: Go ahead and scream.</i><br /> <br /> Bloody Mary in the mirror. The hook-handed man outside your car. The slender figure who flickers across the screen when you\u2019re not quite looking. Urban legends terrify and fascinate in equal measure, passing through whispers and social media posts like a virus of fear with no known point of origin.<br /> <br /> The Scarecrow Minister knows them all by heart; he\u2019s even started a few \u2014 the ones that make you shiver even as you laugh them off. The Minister wants you nice and scared, you see, because there\u2019s safety in fear. Things far more dangerous than bloody ghosts and chilling serial killers lurk in the world\u2019s dark corners, behind mirrors, and just off the path: The Others love to snatch away the curious and unwary. To thwart them, the Minister spreads tales of imaginary terrors so people don\u2019t stumble into the clutches of the real thing.<br /> <br /> <b>Privileges and Duties</b><br /> <br /> The Scarecrow Minister is unsurpassed in spreading fear, able to invoke horror in anyone they meet and ensure any disquieting rumors they spread find fertile minds to worm their way into. But the Minister doesn\u2019t sow fear for fear\u2019s sake; their acts of terror must serve a purpose, like keeping humans from following their curiosity into the awful places where hungry things lurk. To what extremes the Scarecrow Minister will go in the name of their mission varies. Some are content to use psychological warfare and rumors to scare people away from danger. Others take a bloodier approach, reasoning that a well-publicized and grisly murder is the best way to keep foolish humans away from dangerous places, even if the Minister has to wield the knife themself.<br /> <br /> This title is largely a secret one, not only because of the nature of the Scarecrow\u2019s work but also to protect the titleholder. The Gentry and their agents despise the Minister, and plenty of other supernatural predators don\u2019t appreciate potential victims being scared away. Thus, with the notable exception of the Autumn Court, the Scarecrow Minister takes pains to conceal themself from Lost society. With the Leaden Mirror, however, the title brings near-celebrity status, and devotees within the court follow rumors of the Minister\u2019s activities with great interest.<br /> <br /> However, there\u2019s another, darker, reason for this scrutiny. This title isn\u2019t kind to its holder\u2019s Clarity, and sometimes a Minister goes off the rails, losing themself in their role and turning into the kind of horror they\u2019re supposed to be protecting people from. When this happens, it\u2019s the Ashen Court that tracks down the rogue Minister and ensures the title goes to someone more stable.<br /> <br /> <b>Mask and Mien</b><br /> <br /> Ministers who aren\u2019t actively acting like an urban legend dress plainly to avoid notice. The terror-filled tales they spread are never about <i>them</i>, and they often need to disappear quickly after making a scene. However, no matter how inconspicuous they try to make themselves, thick, crude stitching appears on their clothing, and bits of straw poke out of their collar and cuffs.<br /> <br /> The resemblance to a living scarecrow goes even further beneath the Mask, with the Minister developing flat, button-like eyes and thick skin with the texture of old burlap. A Scarecrow Minister who holds the title long enough may even find their head deforming to resemble a jack-o\u2019-lantern, hearing the distant cawing of crows wherever they go.<br /> <br /> <b>Heraldry Token: The Bugbear Mask (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> The Bugbear\u2019s Mask resembles a rubber monster mask, with a faded label marked with the title\u2019s scarecrow-like sigil. When activated while worn, however, the Mask becomes unnervingly real: Crooked fangs glint in the moonlight, sores weep, and patchy fur ripples in the breeze.<br /> <br /> <b>Effects: </b>Every time it\u2019s activated, the Minister can change the Bugbear Mask into any generic monstrous visage they can think of. Alternatively, they can instead spend a Glamour to have the Mask take on the appearance of a specific person or creature they know an onlooker is afraid of.<br /> <br /> [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Catch: </b>The wearer has scared someone they consider an ally or friend in the same scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback: </b>The Mask adheres to the user\u2019s skin. For the rest of the day, it can only be removed with a Strength action, dealing three dice of bashing damage as it tears off.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T14:50:35-08:00","id":1530405,"title":"","content":"I promised <b>Feasts</b>, so let's sit down to dinner.<br /> <br /> One thing we wanted to do with these &quot;other&quot; systems was add a bit of changeling culture outside of the courts. The seemings aren't nearly as cohesive as things like, say, clans for vampires or even auspices for werewolves, but we felt there must be at least a few commonalities between them. Feasts are the Ogres' special system, and it's probably the most straight-up fun of the six. Ogres + food is a recipe for drama. We also liked the idea of bringing a bit of the medieval political banquet/mafia street party vibe to the Gargoyles, who aren't stereotypically as conniving as the other seemings.<br /> <br /> Not much changed in development for this one. The author (a new hire for us) knocked it out of the park from the start. I believe we expanded the systems a bit in second drafts, but this was a really great write-up from the start.<br /> <br /> Tomorrow, I'll be back with another entitlement. Since we're on the subject of Ogres and food, let's check in on what the <b>Knights of the Knowledge of the Tongue </b>are cooking up.<br /> <br /> <b>Feasts: Food and Fightin\u2019</b><br /> <br /> Feasts, in human culture, transcend mere sustenance. Around tables laden with fragrant dishes, we reinforce our bonds, celebrate triumph in battles, and observe sacred rituals. For Ogres whose appetites are altered in sometimes-disturbing ways, truly indulging with compatriots feeds the soul as much as the stomach.<br /> <br /> Behind the fractious nature of the Gargoyles is a desire for acceptance, and Feasts provide them with permission to let down their walls and enjoy each other\u2019s company \u2014 not that there won\u2019t be a little brawling.<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b><br /> <br /> Some say the first Ogre Feasts came out of the Viking tradition, but this is a matter of debate. Many modern-day Bruisers believe this is just an attempt to associate themselves with an oft-romanticized warrior culture, arguing that assuming everything started with Europe is a misinformed way of looking at the world. They offer tales from the Kingdom of Mali in the 1200s, where Timbuktu held a feast that lasted a day and a night before the Ogres undertook a perilous journey into the Sahara. There were also the teahouses in Tang Dynasty China, where Ogres held civilized yet abundant dinners. Perhaps Feasting is as universal a feature of being an Ogre, just as much as their curse and blessing.<br /> <br /> What\u2019s certain is that in 1600s Romania, Summer Queen Milena organized a week-long festival for Gargoyles across Eastern Europe. This became the blueprint for nearly all writing about Feasts. Supposedly, the destruction was so extensive that some freeholds banned Feasting for nearly a century, though Ogres continued to hold them in secret. Historically, the more repressed the rest of the culture was, the more outrageous the Feasts Ogres would throw, with Bruisers trying to outdo each other in feats of consumption and excess to the point that sickness was inevitable and a death or two not unusual.<br /> <br /> Beginning in the 20th century, Feasts became less violent, and guests from other seemings began to be welcomed, something unheard of before. Not everyone was happy with this change, and some believe this waters down what it means to be an Ogre. They call these gatherings derogatory names like \u201cfamily-friendly feasts\u201d or \u201ccorporate cuisine.\u201d In response, these conservatives began holding counter Feasts \u2014 Ogre exclusive, of course, and often gratuitously violent and transgressive.<br /> <br /> <b>Feasting Traditions</b><br /> <br /> The formality of Feasts ranges from potlucks to elaborate banquets. The location, the invitees, the d\u00e9cor \u2014 all of these are important, but they all pale in comparison to the food. The menu and its architects are the key to the success or failure of any Feast, and Ogre chefs are highly sought after. Rumor has it that the celebrated Swiss chef Friedrich the Knife was offered a king\u2019s ransom to leave his freehold for Paris. When he said no, the French sent a team to coerce him by any means necessary. The part about him baking them into a casserole is probably false.<br /> <br /> The food varies depending on the gastronomic needs of the attendees, but it must be made by Ogre hands, either hunted, gathered, or cooked. It\u2019s said that one gentlemanly Gargoyle refused to \u201clower himself\u201d to menial labor and secretly had his wife cook the roast. As soon as he placed it on the ceremonial table, it began to rot. Within minutes, it was covered in maggots and worms, exposing his lies.<br /> <br /> Meat is obligatory \u2014 some cooked, some not. Any Ogre who takes down the game herself is encouraged to proudly display her kill and dramatically retell the story. There\u2019s no such thing as too much bragging at a Feast. But while meat is the centerpiece, it\u2019s far from the only delicacy. Many of the Terrible also appreciate root vegetables, mushrooms, and soft bread to dip in hearty soups. There\u2019s always a table overflowing with desserts. Ogres are encouraged to bring anything unusual they have an appetite for.<br /> <br /> Finding out another Bruiser\u2019s favorite food and bringing it to the Feast is a sign of intense respect, or even courting. One Ogre won the heart of his love by discovering she craved shiny rocks and metals. He presented her with a platter of the finest pyrite and quartz crystals carved to look like fish, with a crust of ground emeralds and a snifter of mercury on the side. The next Feast held in the freehold was in honor of their wedding.<br /> <br /> And what would a Feast be without copious quantities of mead, ale, beer, or wine? Whether it\u2019s a fancy banquet or people eating from troughs, Ogres always bring enough liquor to float an army. More modern Feasts may even have a dedicated bartender, though some older Ogres grumble that this is pretentious; a mug of ale was more than good enough in <i>their</i> day.<br /> <br /> Even the most contentious Ogre puts aside his grudges for a Feast, though that doesn\u2019t mean that they\u2019re pacifistic affairs. On the contrary, brawling is a common enough occurrence that it\u2019s said to be bad luck if a Feast goes by without at least one dust-up. In modern days, these fights never result in more than bruised egos and black eyes, and combatants traditionally have a drink together after they\u2019ve picked themselves up. Ogres often feel rejected for what they are, and being able to appreciate and indulge in their nature is more important to most of them than they\u2019d admit.<br /> <br /> <b>Bruiser Boons</b><br /> <br /> Each Feast receives one to three boons. One is automatic, and another can be added by accumulating 10 successes in an extended action to prepare the Feast (e.g., Dexterity + Crafts for cooking, Presence + Socialize to get the word out, etc.). A third can be added if the Feast has at least fifty attendees.<br /> <br /> The following benefits are available, but Storytellers should feel free to come up with their own:<br /> <br /> <i>Bread and Salt: </i>Used almost exclusively for peace talks, this benefit forces attendees to swear an Oath not to harm each other, physically or otherwise, for the next 24 hours. Within that period, anyone who attempts to negotiate peacefully enjoys a +2 on all Empathy, Persuasion, and Socialize rolls and +1 on all (non-Perception) Composure-based rolls.<br /> <br /> <i>Camaraderie Cuisine: </i>Attendees gain a free Ally dot to represent a connection they made over the food.<br /> <br /> <i>Chef\u2019s Choice: </i>The ultimate cooking contest. Winners of any \u201cbest dish\u201d prizes gain a free dot of Status or Court Goodwill to represent the boost to their reputation.<br /> <br /> <i>Fight It Out: </i>[REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <i>Glamorous Grub: </i>[REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <i>Soothing Sustenance: </i>[REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <i>Winner\u2019s Circle: </i>[REDACTED]<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T17:25:24-08:00","id":1530413,"title":"","content":"Feasts with Chef\u2019s Choice\u2026 the real Cutthroat Kitchen XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T12:40:37-08:00","id":1530468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1530234-book-of-seemings-preview-q-a-coming-next-week?p=1530413#post1530413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feasts with Chef\u2019s Choice\u2026 the real Cutthroat Kitchen XD</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed! Let's sample what the <b>Knights of the Knowledge of the Tongue</b> have on offer.<br /> <br /> The Knights are just an all-around fun concept. They're a much lower-stakes entitlement than the others in the book, which is something we felt like you need in Changeling. We've associated them largely with the Ogres here, and I think that adds an interesting dynamic to their blazon: they're the biggest, meanest, toughest seeming, and they're here to make foie gras (this part gets messy).<br /> <br /> This is one of three legion entitlements in the book (technically four, but one is...tricky). Making them a legion title was a natural choice, and we thought that made their dynamics a little more interesting, especially given that the Knights are often at odds with each other, at least based on all the shouting coming from their kitchen.<br /> <br /> Anyway, here are the Knights of Gastronomy (I got tired of typing out the full name). Tomorrow, let's take a day off, but on Monday I'll be back with something else. Do you all want to see another new system, or would you like to see a couple more kiths?<br /> <br /> <b>Knights of the Knowledge of the Tongue</b><br /> <br /> <i>Seared manticore heart? Pedestrian!</i><br /> <br /> Some might snicker about chefs calling themselves knights \u2014 until they end up on the wrong end of a ladle wielded by an angry Ogre. These changelings, also known as the Knights of Gastronomy, or Epicureans, are more than just foodies: They\u2019re fully committed to finding the most exotic ingredients on both sides of the Hedge and creating taste sensations for the most adventurous eaters in the world. However, unusual for a legion entitlement, the Knights of the Knowledge of the Tongue are almost always at odds with each other. No two Epicureans can ever seem to agree on anything, squabbling over whether the eclairs should feature ectoplasmic or phantasmal cream or if eating centaur meat counts as cannibalism if you only eat the horse half.<br /> <br /> Some members spent time in Arcadia as chefs and are now determined to only cook exactly what they want. Others have always loved food, and now that they\u2019re Lost, they realize an entirely new world of flavors and ingredients is open to them. And for those Ogres with specific dietary requirements, why trust someone else to do a job they can do themselves? They know they can infuse the briarwolf tongues with <i>just</i> the right amount of cayenne to not overpower the dish.<br /> <br /> <b>Privileges and Duties</b><br /> <br /> The Knights of the Knowledge of the Tongue have a simple duty: feed the Lost. Anyone who needs a meal gets one, no questions asked. Anyone who <i>wants </i>one is a different matter. They\u2019re also tasked with experimentation, searching out recipes for the most spectacular meals possible.<br /> <br /> For this, they\u2019re rarely disdained or disliked. At worst, they\u2019re thought of as snobby, and perhaps a touch ridiculous. Most changelings like them, as an entitlement that isn\u2019t invested in adhering to bizarre social mores or mystic traditions is a welcome change. Lost with these gastronomes in their freeholds often approach them for recipe ideas and tips, or even offer great sums to have them cook at their next dinner parties.<br /> <br /> While the Knights are sometimes sought out for Ogre Feasts (p. 115), they often find these gatherings far too focused on quantity over quality. They\u2019d rather nobody taste their creations than for someone to wolf them down without appreciating the flavors. Any Feast that boasts one or more Epicureans despite this is rare indeed, and their presence is widely advertised. Hobs who know of the entitlement bring the Epicureans exotic ingredients, like goblin fruit found only underwater or the whiskers of a bugbear. Of course, they also expect to be able to try the final product.<br /> <br /> When someone joins this order, they vow to never intentionally serve someone food that will taste bad or make them ill. They do sometimes make creations where they\u2019re unsure of the effects, but these are shared among the Epicureans themselves. They have evenings dedicated to trying out each other\u2019s experimental ingredients and dishes, and on these occasions, they always have \u201cantidotes\u201d on hand (like activated charcoal) and never schedule anything important for the next day. On one occasion, a Summer Epicurean used her Regalia to see what would happen if she cooked with pure sunlight. The kitchen was utterly destroyed, but apparently, it did add a delightful zing to her piranha filet.<br /> <br /> <b>Mask and Mien</b><br /> <br /> Those who join this entitlement look as though they enjoy food \u2014 at least a little bit chubby, bright-eyed, and healthy. In their mien, the most obvious change is the tongue. Each Knight\u2019s tongue turns a deep, mystical blue, granting them supernaturally discriminating palates.<br /> <br /> They also, unsurprisingly, smell of food, even behind their Masks. It\u2019s always something pleasant, but the specifics vary from Epicurean to Epicurean: Baked bread is common, as is the scent of a holiday meal. Perfume and cologne can\u2019t cover it up, and indeed, such chemical smells always seem a tad off if a Knight tries to wear one.<br /> <br /> Knights of Gastronomy favor aprons or chef\u2019s jackets even when not cooking, as all are proud of who they are.<br /> <br /> <b>Heraldry Token: The Magical Measuring Spoons (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> To most, this is a normal set of six measuring spoons one would use for baking, each marked with the Knights\u2019 symbol. Even when activated, they don\u2019t appear all that different \u2014 more polished, perhaps, and nestled more together snugly. Each spoon is a different size, and when the chefs work together in a kitchen, they all claim one, though the arguments over who gets which are fierce.<br /> <br /> <b>Effects: </b>When dipped in spices or other substances, the exact amount needed is always captured. There are no spills with these magical spoons; the cook always dispenses the perfect amount. When wielding a spoon, the user gains the rote quality on all cooking actions.<br /> <br /> [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Catch: </b>The user must eat three bites of a food they hate.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback: </b>The user develops hypersensitivity, and her player must make a Resolve + Stamina roll when she\u2019s faced with particularly intense or unpleasant smells, sounds, lights, etc. On a failure, they suffer the Distracted Condition for the scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T17:18:13-08:00","id":1530502,"title":"","content":"The Knights of Gastronomy were one of my favorite old school Entitlements, and the Second Edition version here is excellent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T15:49:23-08:00","id":1530676,"title":"","content":"Alright, since we didn't get a vote on what to do next, let's look at one more entitlement: <b>The Magistrates of the Wax Mask</b>.<br /> <br /> This is <i>not</i> one of our legion entitlements. Not to draw out the mystery too much, but these guys are more/less than they seem, and I think their twist is very <b>Changeling</b> in just the right balance of creepy and whimsical. The basic idea of this entitlement isn't too different from its original incarnation, but the original is also pretty dry, and I like the element of danger/intrigue this one provides. The artist who did the illustration also knocked this one out of the park.<br /> <br /> In development, I believe some minor changes were made to this entitlement's curse (it was originally a bit too much like their Beat condition), but that's about it.<br /> <br /> Here's the Magistrates. Tomorrow, as a last preview before the release, let's do a couple of kiths.<br /> <br /> <b>Magistrates of the Wax Mask</b><br /> <br /> <i>We'll take care of everything.</i><br /> <br /> Wax is malleable. Apply a little heat, and it can be molded into anything, endlessly melted down and reformed. The Magistrates of the Wax Mask strive to be like the substance they\u2019re named for, filling any role and becoming whatever a freehold needs.<br /> <br /> A rather large entitlement at seven members, the Magistrates would call themselves problem-solvers. Each freehold has a variety of rituals, tasks, and celebrations that need to be completed, often annually, to ensure the safety and comfort of its members, but sometimes it lacks the necessary expertise or hands to make these ceremonies work. For a reasonable fee, the Magistrates can provide manpower and whatever skillset is required, from construction projects, to party-planning, to less savory \u2014 but no less necessary \u2014 tasks, all carried out in the shadows.<br /> <br /> Does this dirty work provide this supposedly neutral group of Lost with a great deal of influence over key events in whichever freeholds hire them? Sure, but they\u2019d <i>never</i> dream of taking advantage of the situation. Of course, that\u2019s only because most of the \u201cMagistrates\u201d aren\u2019t capable of dreaming, or thinking at all\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Privileges and Duties</b><br /> <br /> What the people who hire these seven agents don\u2019t realize is that there\u2019s only really one Magistrate. The other six are puppets, wax masks animating store mannequins, anatomical dummies, corpses, or anything else approximately human-shaped.<br /> <br /> The real Magistrate gives these homunculi roles when he affixes their masks. Does the Autumn Court want to host a gala but won\u2019t stoop to asking Spring for help? The Magistrate creates decorators, wait staff, and hosts: They\u2019ll have the guestlist set, dinner catered, and decorations up (in fall colors, of course) before the clock strikes midnight. Does a formal gathering require extra security but the Iron Spear refuses to serve since the guest of honor cheated on the Summer King\u2019s brother? Six bodyguards made to order, each with a gleaming weapon held at the ready. So what if these hirelings are on the quiet side and decidedly unsociable? Are those not the hallmarks of well-trained professionals?<br /> <br /> Magistrates keep the true nature of their coworkers hidden mostly for reasons of avarice. While the title compels service, it also demands compensation, and seven payments going into one set of pockets is too good a deal for most Magistrates to pass up. There\u2019s also the greed of others to consider. To control the Wax Masks is to have half a dozen mutable, unthinkingly loyal servants at one\u2019s beck and call \u2014 a far more attractive prospect to most Wizened than being one of seven titleholders bound to serve the interests of others.<br /> <br /> As long as the Magistrate ensures the jobs he\u2019s hired for are professionally completed, nobody asks questions. And the Wax Masks are nothing if not professional.<br /> <br /> <b>Mask and Mien</b><br /> <br /> The Magistrate\u2019s mien changes in a predictable way: His skin takes on a waxy sheen and becomes slightly malleable, deforming and shifting under pressure or heat. His Mask gets a more subtle treatment, with small flecks and smudges of dried wax manifesting on whatever he wears, no matter how clean he attempts to keep it.<br /> <br /> <b>Heraldry Token: The Wax Masks (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> When not activated, these appear to be a set of seven nearly featureless masks made of hard wax, simple ovals with two holes for eyes and the title\u2019s sigil carved into the back. The only difference the Masks\u2019 miens reveal is that each has a Roman numeral stamped where the mouth should be. The ones bearing the numerals I through VI are Servant Masks, whereas VII is the Master Mask. When activated, the Masks become soft and warm, with the occasional rivulet of half-melted wax running down them.<br /> <br /> <b>Effects: </b>To activate a Servant Mask, it needs to be pressed against the face of a human-shaped effigy while the Magistrate names a one-word profession, like chef, firefighter, or nurse. The token will animate the effigy and grant it an appropriate mask, using the same rules for a changeling strengthening her own Mask. Effigies remain animated for 24 hours and will obey any commands given to them by the wearer of the Master Mask, but only in the context of the profession they\u2019ve been given. Left on their own, Servant Mask effigies will attempt to act out their granted professions as best they can.<br /> <br /> [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Catch:</b><br /> <br /> \u2022 <i>Servant Masks: </i>The user must seal the token to the effigy with his blood, dealing 1 point of bashing damage.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <i>Master Mask: </i>The user must pay each effigy he wishes to command an hour\u2019s worth of the local minimum wage, which he cannot regain: It disappears into the wax.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback:</b><br /> <br /> \u2022 <i>Servant Masks:</i> The effigy\u2019s Mask is imperfect, providing an occasional glimpse of the creature\u2019s true nature to observant eyes.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <i>Master Mask:</i> For any service the user definitively fails to fulfill, the token exacts a price in blood, dealing a point of lethal damage per broken promise.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T16:04:53-08:00","id":1530680,"title":"","content":"A social tradition that's basically a massive gorge-fest feast, <u><i><b>&amp;</b></i></u> an Entitlement based upon making exotic foods? <span style=\"font-size:72px\"><u><i><b>ME LIKEY-DIKEY!!!!!!!!</b></i></u></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T20:30:13-08:00","id":1530704,"title":"","content":"Okay, as a proper vote this time, I'd like to see a new system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-13T00:35:55-08:00","id":1530721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1530234-book-of-seemings-preview-q-a-coming-next-week?p=1530704#post1530704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, as a proper vote this time, I'd like to see a new system.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean by a new system?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-13T04:46:14-08:00","id":1530735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1530234-book-of-seemings-preview-q-a-coming-next-week?p=1530721#post1530721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean by a new system?</div> </div> </div> </div>As in the six seeming-specific systems introduced in this book, of which Feasts have currently been previewed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-13T07:56:59-08:00","id":1530741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1530234-book-of-seemings-preview-q-a-coming-next-week?p=1530704#post1530704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, as a proper vote this time, I'd like to see a new system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25281-coachman","name":"Coachman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25281_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-13T13:10:55-08:00","id":1530751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1530234-book-of-seemings-preview-q-a-coming-next-week?p=1530704#post1530704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, as a proper vote this time, I'd like to see a new system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw this slightly too late, so I'll do one of those tomorrow!<br /> <br /> Today, let's check in on the Fairest, along with one of their kiths.<br /> <br /> I don't have much commentary here apart from saying that the chapter this excerpt is from was part of our efforts to tease out the character of each seeming a bit more. We don't usually do wholly narrative chapters in our books, but the seemings don't have quite as much meat on the bone or history as, say, the clans do in <b>Requiem</b>. So, we wanted to provide some guidance on what makes each seeming tick. This is only one part of a longer section.<br /> <br /> Tomorrow, I'll be back with another excerpt after the book drops: <b>Looking Glasses</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest</b><br /> <br /> <i>Please stay for another drink! I don\u2019t like what I see when I\u2019m alone.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Who We Used to Be</b><br /> <br /> We were singers, trophy wives, heartthrobs, and politicians. We were used to being treated like we were special for things we couldn\u2019t control. We\u2019re not always beautiful, but there\u2019s always something about us. They call us \u201cMuses,\u201d but what we use to inspire could be anything from an enchanting voice to a snappy fashion sense. We had what everyone wanted. Money, beauty, talent, friends. It\u2019s trendy to act like people with privilege have nothing to complain about, to sneer about \u201cpoor little rich girls.\u201d Some of us <i>do</i> deserve that. Many Fairest have an arrogant, entitled streak a mile long.<br /> <br /> Then there\u2019s the beautiful ballerina who lost her childhood to endless hours of practice, considered a failure by 22 because she was never quite good enough to be the lead. There\u2019s the rich boy who charms everyone in his wake, but if his father\u2019s political enemies find out their rival\u2019s son is a queer, he can\u2019t be sure his father won\u2019t choose his career over his heir. Everyone\u2019s got <i>something</i><b>.</b><br /> <br /> We were taken for our talents, but it\u2019s our weaknesses the Gentry exploit. Humans are social animals, no matter how much misanthropy might be in vogue, and most Fairest need people. Perhaps it\u2019s more accurate to say we need to be needed. Are we worth anything at all if we don\u2019t sparkle? How would we even know?<br /> <br /> <i>Alistair:</i> Born into poverty in early-20th-century New York, Alistair began rumrunning when he was 15. By the time he was 20, Prohibition was in full swing, and he was working for one of the most dangerous smuggling gangs in the Northeast. He took too many risks but got away with it through his combination of looks, charm, and practiced sincerity. It was impossible not to smile back at him, no matter what ridiculous plan he might be spinning.<br /> <br /> <i>Esperanza: </i>She didn\u2019t mean to be snobby. It wasn\u2019t her fault if the people around her were terribly irritating. She\u2019d sneer at anyone she considered not worth her time, and with just a look, she could wither every ounce of your self-esteem. Sometimes she used this to get creeps to leave her friends alone, but her judgmental eyes would too often fall upon an overworked barista or tired mother whose children weren\u2019t being quiet enough.<br /> <br /> <i>Ian:</i> He wanted to be a world-renowned violinist, and as a child prodigy, it seemed like that goal was well within reach. But the older he got, the less his talent was special. Oh, he was certainly <i>good</i>, but an adult playing the violin doesn\u2019t get nearly as much praise as a child. And there just wasn\u2019t that much money in it. In truth, he wanted to quit \u2014 but he was afraid that it was the only thing he\u2019d ever be any good at.<br /> <br /> <b>The Beautiful Nightmare</b><br /> <br /> For us, one of the worst things about Arcadia was the moments of wonder and pleasure. Many of us don\u2019t wish to speak of our experiences with the Wizened who was forced to sew until her fingers bled, or the Beast who had his legs broken and reformed when he couldn\u2019t run fast enough. We\u2019re often met with scorn, with others saying we\u2019re whining when our torments consist of performing at soir\u00e9es.<br /> <br /> Our horrors were almost always subtle. We were treated as a favored friend, pet, or lover \u2014 until the Gentry got bored of us and tossed us away, or just forgot about us. This often cycled, and we\u2019d crave our Keeper\u2019s attention as much as we feared it. We remember, to our shame, that we weren\u2019t always chained up or kept in a cage. Instead, we were plied with fine foods and given infusions of ecstasy that, even half-remembered, have us waking in the night fevered and guilty. Fairest are most likely to have had a sexual aspect to our durances. Sometimes our Keepers took us as lovers, or even spouses; stereotypical human roles amuse them. One plays the role of \u201cfather\u201d in a twisted <i>Leave It to Beaver</i> spectacle. Others have much darker tales.<br /> <br /> Our bodies weren\u2019t twisted; instead, we were <i>perfected</i>. Flaws removed \u2014 features exaggerated or minimized based on our Keeper\u2019s desires. Some of us now lack the ability to make an unpleasant expression or even raise our voices. Some Gentry sculpt us to be mirrors of themselves. Perhaps for a performance, or so the Fae can use one of us as a spare face to try on clothes or new hairstyles. It may not compare to working in the mines or bleeding on a battlefield, but there\u2019s a special kind of suffering that comes from seeing your tormentor\u2019s face every time you look in the mirror.<br /> <br /> <i>Alistair:</i> He was taken to the Palace of Unearthly Delights by the Princess of Flames and Sighs to entertain her guests. The more he pleased them, the more rewards he received from his Keeper. It became as easy as breathing for him to see who wanted only a light flirtation with her wine and who wanted him as a bedwarmer for the night. When the Princess went into one of her dark moods, there were no more parties, of course, and she would often forget to feed her vassals. But when she smiled, the world transformed into dances and light.<br /> <br /> <i>Esperanza:</i> The Lord of the Killing Frost was handsome, wealthy, and had perfect manners, and he took Esperanza to his Citadel of Crystal Winter to be the perfect consort. She was treated like glass, but every day he allowed a little less freedom. When she resisted even a little or showed any sign of unhappiness, it was her servants who were punished instead of her.<br /> <br /> <i>Ian:</i> The Court of Disgrace and Vilification was an awful parody of a chivalric society. The Last Knight-Errant snatched Ian after a concert as a new \u201cperformer,\u201d and he was made to play the violin while being constantly heckled. All day, courtiers would throw things at the performers. The insults they shouted took physical form and helped mold the captives into more perfect entertainers. Bitterness infused Ian day after day, and he learned to survive by becoming as vicious as the worst of them.<br /> <br /> <b>Treasured (Fairest)</b><br /> <br /> <i>Didn\u2019t anyone tell you it\u2019s rude to stare?</i><br /> <br /> Faeries are fascinated by beauty, but what they deem beautiful is anyone\u2019s guess. These changelings were already exceptional in some way: exceedingly tall, strikingly blond, symmetrically built, or whatever else a specific Other favored. The Treasured might be lured with flattery and adoration, or maybe other humans never appreciated their uniqueness.<br /> <br /> Once captive, the True Fae exaggerates this quality further, sometimes to grotesque (by human standards) degrees. When satisfied with the results, this living <i>objet d\u2019art</i> is placed on display for fellow Gentry to admire. Gentry stroll through galleries of Treasured captives, enjoying them as humans would paintings or sculptures. Others probe or examine specimens under glass or behind zoo bars. The Treasured\u2019s sole purpose is to be observed.<br /> <br /> Fashions change, though. The Keeper might choose a new theme for the gallery, or keeping alabaster changelings may become pass\u00e9. Thus, the Treasured gets packed away in the vault and forgotten, or discarded with all the other broken toys. But once their Keeper\u2019s watchful eyes are turned elsewhere, a Treasured can slink away, finally out of everyone\u2019s sight.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, many Treasured still get stares after they return. Humans glimpse something exceptional about them, even if they can\u2019t see through their Masks, and other changelings can\u2019t help but be riveted. They see the true mien, and that kind of \u201cperfection\u201d is hard to ignore. It leaves Treasured second-guessing the sincerity of others\u2019 interest in them. But don\u2019t let looks fool you \u2014 they\u2019re keen to prove they\u2019re much more than pretty faces.<br /> <br /> <b>Kith Blessing</b><br /> <br /> When a Treasured uses Socialize to capture or hold the attention of a subject who can see them, achieving three successes counts as an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> <i>Timeless Trend: </i>[REDACTED]<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-13T23:18:29-08:00","id":1530785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1530234-book-of-seemings-preview-q-a-coming-next-week?p=1530751#post1530751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I saw this slightly too late, so I'll do one of those tomorrow!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thankee much.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, The Fairest were always of a strong interest, and in recent years grew to be my favorite Seeming, and I'm glad to see the roots that Winter Masques still show strong in the sample, while getting teased out in different directions. Not looking forward to having to work tomorrow with this out at the same time-I'll have to see if I can sneak read between cases. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T12:18:07-08:00","id":1530834,"title":"","content":"And here we go:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/470934/Book-of-Seemings?affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Book of Seemings</b></a><br /> <br /> Discount/previous buyer bundles:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/470935/Lost-and-Resurrected-BUNDLE?affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Book of Seemings + Bloodlines: The Resurrected</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/470936/Lost-in-Rome-BUNDLE?affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Book of Seemings + Requiem for Rome 2E</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/470937/Lost-in-Time-BUNDLE?affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Book of Seemings + Bloodlines: The Ageless</b></a><br /> <br /> <i><b><u>NMD PATREON: </u></b></i><a href=\"http://patreon.com/NoneMoreDarkPublishing\" target=\"_blank\"><u><b><i>patreon.com/NoneMoreDarkPublishing</i></b></u></a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T15:47:15-08:00","id":1530852,"title":"","content":"Alright, I promised an excerpt, so let's gaze into the <b>Looking Glasses</b>.<br /> <br /> \u200bOne of the reasons I like these so much is that they're very different from what you expect for the Fairest. They're a little creepier and more sinister than this seeming usually gets, and I think that's a fun way to expand on their themes. I also just love the old magic mirror trope, and I think the author did a great job of integrating them into the Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Not much preamble today, but I'll be back tomorrow with something about the new antagonists in the book: <b>The Forgotten</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Looking Glasses: </b><b>Through a Mirror, Fabulously</b><br /> <br /> <i>The mirror sits neglected in its corner, covered in dust. Nevertheless, you feel drawn to it, as your own reflection seems to beckon you. You dust off the surface and see yourself within it, more striking than you ever thought possible. You take the mirror and place it somewhere secret. You know, somehow, that no one deserves to look upon it but you.</i><br /> <br /> <i>One day, while brushing your hair, you ask the mirror a question and it answers back. Not in words, but in images. Visions of what might be? These omens dance across your mind while you sleep, impossible to forget. Some of them come true.</i><br /> <br /> <i>You gaze into the mirror more and more, the world\u2019s reflection growing more enticing than reality. Your motley wonders where you\u2019ve gone.</i><br /> <br /> <i>One day, you ask it to find something for you. To see someone. Your fetch, an old friend, a lost love, an enemy\u2026 and it shows you what you seek. You spend hours, days even, watching the object of your growing obsession. You pour over their every waking moment. You waste away while your reflection becomes even more beautiful.</i><br /> <br /> <i>One day, you ask to see your Keeper, and you are never heard from again.</i><br /> <br /> Since the first Fairest was stolen into Arcadia, mirrors have loved them. They shine and preen and make such beautiful reflections. As the Muses wept through their durances, their mirrors kept them company, and it\u2019s said the mirror world itself became besotted with these poor souls and offered them a gift. And Sovereigns know better than to refuse a gift.<br /> <br /> All Fairest can create Looking Glasses. By pouring attention into any object with a clear, reflective surface, a Muse can transform it into a Looking Glass. In fact, it\u2019s so easy that many of these mirrors are created by accident \u2014 which is part of why they\u2019re so dangerous.<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b><br /> <br /> The first gift the mirror grants is the future. If asked, a Looking Glass can show its creator visions of what\u2019s to come. Its prophecies are always heavy with symbolism, difficult to interpret, but inevitably true. But the more you ask, the more you <i>want</i> to ask. The Looking Glass worms its way into your thoughts more often than you\u2019d like, until you become fixated on it.<br /> <br /> Once a Muse develops an obsession with her mirror, she can unlock its real power. She can ask it to show her the smartest person in the freehold, her ideal lover, or her fetch. Friends, partners, foes \u2014 the mirror can show her all of them. She just has to ask.<br /> <br /> And she will, again and again, until the mirror and the people reflected in it are all she can think about. Maybe she starts missing meals. Maybe she starts tearing out her hair when she\u2019s away from the mirror too long. Maybe she starts stalking the people she spies on. Maybe she doesn\u2019t do anything anymore but gaze at her own reflection. By then, the mirror has her, and as her body decays, her reflection only grows more and more radiant. Perhaps, when she\u2019s dead, her reflection will walk off into the world without her. Beautiful and perfect.<br /> <br /> <b>Obsessed with Myself</b><br /> <br /> It\u2019s common wisdom among the Fairest to never make a Looking Glass. But how often does wisdom prevail? Looking Glasses are dangerous, but their power is tempting. Who doesn\u2019t want to know the future? Who wouldn\u2019t want to know their enemy\u2019s every move? Who doesn\u2019t want to find their true love? Few would admit to creating a Looking Glass, and even fewer would describe themselves as addicts. The Fairest know you don\u2019t <i>talk</i> about the mirrors; you just watch for signs of dependence and take the object away if you can.<br /> <br /> Opinions on Looking Glasses vary from freehold to freehold. Some ignore them, some pretend not to use them, and some allow their use only under supervision. Some courts will keep a few mirror addicts around and feed their habits in exchange for information. Looking Glasses can be exceptional tools of war, particularly against other changelings, and if these mirrors are common in a freehold, hobs might sell charms and wards against them in nearby Goblin Markets.<br /> <br /> A few freeholds take a zero-tolerance stance, shattering every Looking Glass they can find for fear that the Gentry might see someone watching and step through.<br /> <br /> <b>Through the Looking Glass</b><br /> <br /> Few changelings know how or why Looking Glasses work. They assume it\u2019s another aspect of the Wyrd playing tricks on the Fairest, but the truth is far stranger.<br /> <br /> Whenever a Looking Glass is created, it acts as a beacon to creatures in mirror space, who flock to it to admire the Fairest who created it. Looking Glasses allow mirror creatures to see beyond the frame of a mirror and into the future, granting them glimpses of the people the object spies upon. This is a wondrous thrill to mirror folk, and they shower their love and attention on the Muse who offers them such freedom. It\u2019s just that their affection is rather addictive. Who doesn\u2019t want a captive audience?<br /> <br /> If one of the Fairest dies from starvation or neglect while obsessing over their Looking Glass, a mirror creature steps through the mirror and takes the body into the mirror space to honor them with a grand funeral. Others say the mirror creature steps through and <i>becomes</i> the deceased changeling, transforming at last from reflection to reality.<br /> <br /> Mirror folk loathe when humans steal Looking Glasses and abuse their powers. Ugly mortals were never meant to have them, and are punished harshly for their transgression against the Muses. Only perfection is worthy, and no human soul can have that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T08:34:16-08:00","id":1530903,"title":"","content":"So, I bought the book and couldn't be happier with it! I especially like the additional Seeming Blessings and would love to see some for the Contracts in Kith and Kin (I am terrible at making up seeming blessings).<br /> <br /> I read the Elemental blessing for Dance of the Toys and can't get &quot;fire-breathing stapler&quot; out of my head now! XD<br /> <br /> I do have a question regarding Font Attunement. Offering the three sacrifices at the season change will increase your influence by how many dots? One? Also, can the sacrifice be repeated at the next season change to further increase Influence? Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25281-coachman","user":"Coachman","date":". 02-15-2024, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25281-coachman","name":"Coachman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25281_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T13:12:26-08:00","id":1530923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coachman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1530234-book-of-seemings-preview-q-a-coming-next-week?p=1530903#post1530903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I bought the book and couldn't be happier with it! I especially like the additional Seeming Blessings and would love to see some for the Contracts in Kith and Kin (I am terrible at making up seeming blessings).<br /> <br /> I read the Elemental blessing for Dance of the Toys and can't get &quot;fire-breathing stapler&quot; out of my head now! XD<br /> <br /> I do have a question regarding Font Attunement. Offering the three sacrifices at the season change will increase your influence by how many dots? One? Also, can the sacrifice be repeated at the next season change to further increase Influence? Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one dot and repeatable? <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> wrote that section, I believe, so he might be able to field that question better than I!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T13:23:42-08:00","id":1530926,"title":"","content":"Alright, I promised we'd discuss the <b>Forgotten </b>today, so let's take a look outside of biting range.<br /> <br /> Like our clan books, we wanted to include antagonists, but because we were doing a book of <i>all </i>the seemings, we wanted to do a more cohesive group of horrors. And what better way to do that than through a mirror darkly?<br /> <br /> The Forgotten are what happens when a changeling escapes Arcadia but can't quite get through the Thorns. Instead of Clarity, they must restore their minds by eating mortal (and changeling) flesh. These quasi-changelings have their own seemings like the Lost, and favor a special Regalia called Maw. I'll let the write-up do the talking here, but I really like these characters. They add a bit of that visceral quality a lot of old fairytales share. This is probably the section of the book I picked over the most post-development. Mostly that was simplifying a few things for each Forgotten seeming and generally cleaning some systems. I think they turned out wonderfully, and I hope you all have fun unleashing them on your chronicles.<br /> <br /> <b>The Forgotten: The Hungry Ones</b><br /> <br /> When a changeling slips free of their durance, they must flee through the Hedge as the Thorns try to tear away the tattered remains of their soul, trying to remove the last fragments of the changeling\u2019s connection to the human world. Those who weather this assault and make it out the other side become Lost. The ones who survive the physical wounds but lose their identities \u2014 their selves \u2014 are Forgotten.<br /> <br /> Forgotten are rare, but they have a devastating impact on those who encounter them. With their human essence obliterated, they\u2019re left with a terrible hunger that can only ever be temporarily sated by consuming human flesh, a wretched attempt to regain what the Thorns took from them. Shunned by both changelings and other denizens of the Hedge, most live in isolation, emerging only to feed.<br /> <br /> Lost scholars theorize that the Forgotten are the origin of many of the cannibalistic horrors found in folklore around the world. What do Scandinavian trolls, Japanese kappa, and Scottish kelpies have in common? They all want to eat you.<br /> <br /> <b>Systems</b><br /> <br /> Forgotten come in as many individual varieties as the Lost themselves, but they have a few universal traits that set them apart from their less monstrous cousins. Treat Hungry Ones as Lost except as outlined below.<br /> <br /> <b>Seeming and Kith</b><br /> <br /> The Forgotten possess their own seemings, reflecting the sort of Lost they might have become if only they had finished their journey home. However, theirs are twisted, violent echoes that instead focus on methods of hunting and devouring prey. They are discussed in greater detail in the following sections.<ul><li>Disasters (Elementals)</li> <li>Imps (Darklings)</li> <li>Knockers (Wizened)</li> <li>Sirens (Fairest)</li> <li>Stalkers (Beasts)</li> <li>Trolls (Ogres)</li> </ul>Hungry Ones develop the same kiths as the Lost.<br /> <br /> <b>Anchors and Clarity</b><br /> <br /> Forgotten have no Threads, only Needles. They also have no Clarity or Touchstones. As such, they are immune to any ability that affects Clarity, and they have no seeming curse (being Forgotten is more than enough). Hungry Ones can use kenning, but it is always a chance die.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing</b><br /> <br /> Each Forgotten seeming gains a unique blessing, rawer in power than those of their changeling counterparts but often more sinister. Unlike the Lost, Hungry Ones don\u2019t gain an additional Attribute dot at character creation, but neither do these blessings have any catch.<br /> <br /> <b>Prey and Lure</b><br /> <br /> Each Forgotten gains a favored form of <b>Prey </b>and a <b>Lure </b>to draw them in. These qualities vary between seemings and are discussed in their respective entries.<br /> <br /> The Prey is the Forgotten\u2019s preferred meal, the specific kind of person they crave more than any other. If a Hungry One eats someone who counts as Prey, living or dead, she completely refills her Glamour pool.<br /> <br /> The Lure is the way the Forgotten attract or trap victims, a preferred method of isolating them or drawing them into the depths of the Hedge. Anyone who counts as Prey suffers the Forgotten\u2019s Wyrd score as a penalty (to a limit of five) to resist or otherwise see through any action that aligns with her Lure, including the use of Contracts.<br /> <br /> <b>Glamour</b><br /> <br /> Hungry Ones have only a terrible emptiness where the remains of humanity should be, and it eats away at them with each passing day. Forgotten lose 1 Glamour every sunrise. However, time is inconsistent in the Hedge; weeks in the mortal world might pass between losses, or a Hungry One who appeared full and rational only yesterday may emerge ravenous and snarling tomorrow.<br /> <br /> Forgotten can only regain Glamour by consuming the flesh of changelings, hobgoblins, and humans. Every time a Hungry One inflicts damage with a bite attack on any creature with a Glamour track, she also steals a point of Glamour from her victim\u2019s pool. Alternatively, if she consumes a changeling or hob\u2019s fresh corpse, she gains Glamour equal to their victim\u2019s Size or Wyrd, whichever is less. The Forgotten can\u2019t steal Glamour from mortals, but consuming a fresh human corpse grants Glamour equal to half their total capacity, rounded up. Forgotten gain the most Glamour from eating their Prey (see above).<br /> <br /> Beyond their insatiable craving for human and fae flesh, the Forgotten require no other sustenance. They don\u2019t need to sleep, drink, or consume any other source of food. Hungry Ones don\u2019t age normally and will generally persist until someone kills them or they starve to death.<br /> <br /> <b>Forgetting</b><br /> <br /> As Hungry Ones don\u2019t possess Clarity, they can\u2019t even escape the horror of their own existence in the ecstasy of madness. Instead, a Forgotten\u2019s level of rationality is based on when they last ate. All Forgotten suffer from the Amnesia Condition as a result of having the majority of their human identities torn away by the Thorns; this Condition can never be resolved but is temporarily suppressed whenever a Hungry One has a full Glamour pool.<br /> <br /> If a Forgotten\u2019s Glamour pool is at least half-full, she can spend a Willpower to temporarily suppress Amnesia for a scene. If she has less than half her Glamour pool remaining, she also gains the Deprived Condition. Finally, if a Forgotten has no Glamour in her pool, she gains the Berserk Condition, which cannot be resolved until she regains Glamour by consuming a fresh meal.<br /> <br /> <b>Hedge-Bound</b><br /> <br /> With their humanity almost completely ripped away by the Thorns, the mortal world rejects the Forgotten, and the Hedge becomes their home. Hungry Ones count as hobgoblins for the purposes of navigating the Hedge and being in the mortal world <b>(Changeling: The Lost</b>, p. 253<b>)</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Regalia</b><br /> <br /> A Forgotten\u2019s affinity Contracts are its equivalent seeming\u2019s favored Regalia plus Maw (below). However, some Hungry Ones can access independent Contracts (<b>Kith and Kin</b>, p. 58). Only members of the relevant Forgotten seeming and their Lost counterparts can develop them. In the latter case, normal changelings must have a Forgotten tutor, as per Pupil\u2019s Devotion.<br /> <br /> <b>New Regalia: Maw</b><br /> <br /> A maw is different from a mouth. A mouth opens to eat, certainly, but it also frowns, kisses, smiles, pouts, and reflects the person it\u2019s a part of in myriad other ways. A <i>maw </i>does none of this: It\u2019s gnashing teeth and wet lips that open to a dark, gaping gullet. A maw symbolizes constant hunger, an insatiable need to consume without ceasing. It represents both a terrible ending and an endless desire.<br /> <br /> Maw Contracts are almost unknown among the Lost, save for a few Ogres, Beasts, and Gristlegrinders who can\u2019t quite forget the crunch of bone between their molars. However, every Forgotten feels an instinctive connection to Maw as their hunger for flesh claws at their ragged minds.<br /> <br /> Seeming benefits apply to both the listed Lost seeming and its Forgotten equivalent.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T10:22:46-08:00","id":1530986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1530234-book-of-seemings-preview-q-a-coming-next-week?p=1530923#post1530923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think one dot and repeatable? <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> wrote that section, I believe, so he might be able to field that question better than I!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the intention was one dot and repeatable. You can get yourself all the way up to five dots of Influence, but it takes time and you are going to have to work to maintain it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T14:27:40-08:00","id":1531003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1530234-book-of-seemings-preview-q-a-coming-next-week?p=1530986#post1530986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the intention was one dot and repeatable. You can get yourself all the way up to five dots of Influence, but it takes time and you are going to have to work to maintain it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll make sure to make that more explicit in the errata!<br /> <br /> Alright, let's look at another entitlement: <b>The Lost Pantheon</b>.<br /> <br /> In a way, this entitlement is probably the closest structurally to its original incarnation. It breaks the rule about legion entitlements having no more than six members, instead suggesting that there's no doubling up on the godly personae these changelings can adopt: only on Zeus, Thor, etc. That said, you could interpret that as this being many, many, <i>many </i>entitlements with similar tokens, but that's up to you.<br /> <br /> One change I quite like from the original is presenting these changelings as being a bit more self-aware. Members of the 1E Lost Pantheon really did think they were gods, or at least that <i>changelings </i>were gods, and while that might be true of some members in 2E, many/most see themselves as avatars of deities rather than literally being them. The entitlement's stronger focus on individual, named gods is also a bit different from the original, but that made more sense within the structure of 2E entitlements, where your character embodies a particular role.<br /> <br /> With that, here's the Lost Pantheon. Tomorrow, let's look at the Ogres' Forgotten mirror: the <b>Trolls</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>The Lost Pantheon</b><br /> <br /> <i>Where have all the old gods gone? We\u2019re right here.</i><br /> <br /> All myths sprang from the gods. Once, they were worshiped throughout the world, but as science and technology winnowed away belief in their power, they slipped into dreams and dusty tomes. Babylonian, Egyptian, Greek, Norse\u2026 their empires have fallen. Their domains have been left untended for too long. They are all forgotten.<br /> <br /> But not the Lost Pantheon. By taking on godly guises, its members raise divine hands to ensure souls are ferried, new ground is consecrated, and inspiration is meted out to the worthy. Along the way, they restore faith in a world left wanting. The wait has been long, but now, the Ancients wake.<br /> <br /> <b>Privileges and Duties</b><br /> <br /> Unlike most legion titles, the Lost Pantheon theoretically has no limit on its membership, for as long as humans have gods, the Pantheon can stand for them. However, only one Ancient can represent a given deity: one Baldur, one Juno, one Horus. Still, few know how many are embodied within this entitlement at present, and it\u2019s rare for a freehold to have more than one member in its bounds. When they do cross paths, they\u2019re more likely to come to blows over mythological grudges than they are to work together.<br /> <br /> The specific duties of each Pantheon member vary with the godly roles they take on, but every domain includes the following: the maintenance of at least one Elemental Font (p. 118), preserving or stoking its presence within the Hedge and keeping the paths open so its power can flow into the mortal world; maintaining at least one temple, such as restoring a ruin from antiquity, consecrating a Hollow, or running gatherings for initiates; and protecting the interests and safety of a dedicated type of follower (children, mothers, farmers, scholars, etc.).<br /> <br /> Wherever an Ancient wanders, they must uphold their deity\u2019s ideals. To embody Artemis, one must forswear the touch of men and join in the hunt; to embody Idunn, one must tend and defend an orchard of goblin fruit. Thus elevated, they attract prayer, and pilgrims seek them to resolve issues within their purview. A member of the Lost Pantheon might rescue an injured animal sacred to them, take in a child orphaned by an eruption of their element, or protect a changeling member of the profession they bless.<br /> <br /> To better carry out their divine duties, their capacity for the fantastic deepens. Events that might shake another\u2019s Clarity merely force them to reconsider. The Gates of Ivory stand forever open, their consciousnesses alert whether their flesh wakes or sleeps.<br /> <br /> <b>Mask and Mien</b><br /> <br /> An Ancient\u2019s Mask makes them appear larger than life or enchantingly beautiful, or perhaps they strike terror into mortal hearts. Depending on how magnanimous they are, they may fill others with wonder, terror, or submission.<br /> <br /> The precise nature of an Ancient\u2019s mien depends on which traits their godly self most favors: Poseidon\u2019s armored scales, Hathor\u2019s cow-horn crown, Chantico\u2019s molten magma hair. These traits grow more extreme the more steeped in the Wyrd she becomes.<br /> <br /> If this sounds unsettlingly like the Gentry, they\u2019re glad you noticed. Members of the Lost Pantheon disagree on the precise nature of the Fae and how they relate to the gods, but the Ancients feel their power and ability to create are worth emulating \u2014 if not their methods.<br /> <br /> <b>Heraldry Token: The Celestial Medallions (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> In its Mask, a Celestial Medallion resembles an old, battered coin or some other metallic token from antiquity, usually from the nation where the Ancient\u2019s god originated. Behind the Mask, it\u2019s a glorious electrum star with nine points, its central motif representing a specific deity incorporated into the entitlement\u2019s heraldry (Athena\u2019s Aegis, Thor\u2019s Mjolnir, etc.). No two are exactly alike.<br /> <br /> <b>Effects: </b>Unlike most heraldry tokens, a Celestial Medallion can\u2019t be stolen, at least not for long. The Wyrd ensures it returns to its rightful keeper\u2019s hand within 24 hours of its removal.<br /> <br /> Those who look upon the Medallion know the truth of its owner\u2019s divinity. If they\u2019re already faithful, they know they look upon the avatar of their god, but even if they aren\u2019t yet initiated, they feel significant awe. The bearer of the Celestial Medallion gains the 8-again quality on any attempt to make a first impression with a human, and this increases to the rote quality if the human worships the god she\u2019s embodying. (<i>Conditional</i>)<br /> <br /> [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Catch: </b>The Medallion must be immersed in or passed through the element associated with its current bearer for one hour as the user recites prayers.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback: </b>For the rest of the day, the bearer sees the Wyrd in everything, bombarded by elemental illusions, inverses of character or nature, and grim (possibly true) fates. She gains the Distracted Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-17T13:14:27-08:00","id":1531033,"title":"","content":"Today, let's take a look at one of the Forgotten seemings: The Trolls.<br /> <br /> The Trolls are the dark mirrors of the Ogres. I'll mostly let the write-up speak for itself here, but I think these are my favorite of the six &quot;anti-seemings.&quot; They have a fun connection to fairytale monsters, yet they're also the Forgotten who can <i>kind of </i>deal with the Lost on less violent terms (relatively speaking). I also think their sample character is wonderfully tragic/horrifying.<br /> <br /> Not much to add here! Tomorrow, let's look at another Forgotten seeming: the <b>Knockers</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Troll: A Tale of Avarice</b><br /> <br /> Trolls are monstrous, cannibalistic cousins to the Ogres. Where Ogres often have gruesome appetites, a Troll\u2019s hunger is a howling, bottomless pit. They are doomed to hunt eternally for more meat and more treasures, for Trolls can feed off the wealth they extort from others just as well as can they chew on your bones. But no fortune, however vast, is ever enough to truly sate them.<br /> <br /> <b>Once</b><br /> <br /> Most Ogres grow to despise the relentless violence their Keepers force them to inflict, feeling deeply ashamed of the gruesome appetites cultivated in them. They want to be forgiven, to make amends, or revel in their newfound freedom. Trolls escape their masters, but never unlearn their Keepers\u2019 lessons. They free themselves from violence, but can\u2019t stop inflicting it. But there are many ways for an Ogre to lose their way and become a Troll: Some refuse to return on the cusp of escape, too ashamed of the horrors they inflicted on the Gentry\u2019s behalf. Some chose to stay, finding the taste of living flesh too delectable to ever quit the habit. And still others decide they\u2019re owed something, deciding to take what\u2019s theirs by any means necessary.<br /> <br /> Unlike their Forgotten kin, Trolls don\u2019t track down their prey: They wait for it to come to them. Trolls haunt bridges, trods, Hedge gates, and places rich in natural resources, licking their lips when unsuspecting morsels wander too close. Most are happy enough to eat whoever wanders by, but their hunger can also sometimes be sated with riches and tokens, so cunning hobs and changelings bargain in exchange for safe passage. If the offer\u2019s good enough, the Troll might even decide not to eat you \u2014 but that\u2019s never a guarantee.<br /> <br /> Despite their ragged appearances and uncouth table manners, Trolls often amass enormous treasure hoards from their tolls. New Trolls bury their trinkets near their haunts, while the eldest of them build palaces around the bridges and pathways they guard, stuffed with tokens and baubles and delicate things their clumsy hands might break. When Trolls are hungry (which is most of the time), they quite enjoy their lot in life. They revel in their riches, power, and cravings. Now that they\u2019re free of their Keepers, who they can barely recall, they can indulge however they like. More flesh, more stuff, more violence\u2026 Just <i>more</i>, forever after.<br /> <br /> Until they over-indulge, regain their hazy memories, and recall all the faces they\u2019ve hurt and how they tasted on their teeth. Trolls often fall into deep depressions when they\u2019re sated, leaving their bridges unguarded to sob into their treasures.<br /> <br /> <b>Prey</b><br /> <br /> Trolls prey on the<b> prosperous</b>. Something in their hearts is made whole by devouring those who have more than they need, and they consider flesh from the rich to be a treasure equal to gold. Trolls can smell meat and money and draw power by hoarding them. As Trolls grow hungrier, they grow taller, wider, and stronger, and when starving, they can grow as big as a barn. This increased size only fuels their hunger, as Trolls need more flesh and wealth to sustain their massive frames.<br /> <br /> <b>Lure</b><br /> <br /> Though their gnashing teeth and gigantic statures are frightening enough, a Troll\u2019s <b>paths</b> are what truly terrify changelings. Trolls may deny passage to anyone who wants to cross their path, use their bridge, or open their gates, making it impossible for anyone to navigate around them. If you encounter a Troll on your path, you\u2019ll never reach your destination unless you pay, kill, or outsmart the monster barring your way. Your only other option is to give up the quest altogether \u2014 which might be the only path that leads to survival.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing</b><br /> <br /> All Trolls gain the Giant Merit. When one has the Amnesia Condition, he gains two levels of Size and Speed. When he has the Berserk Condition, increase these traits by another two levels. These increases improve derived Advantages as normal and are lost when the appropriate Conditions are suppressed or resolved. The Troll can suppress this transformation for a scene by spending a Glamour, but he can also take an instant action to regain it.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, Trolls gain Glamour when people pay them to avoid being eaten or hurt: one Glamour per dot of a token or Availability rating of a mundane item. This nourishes them like flesh, and the richer the payment, the more filling it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 02-17-2024, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-17T15:01:54-08:00","id":1531036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1530234-book-of-seemings-preview-q-a-coming-next-week?p=1531033#post1531033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think their sample character is wonderfully tragic/horrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>The name is also extremely Soulsborne-y, upon reflection, which is apropos.<br /> <br /> <i>Visceral</i> is definitely the right word for what the Forgotten bring to the game; Changeling has one of the &quot;cleaner&quot; baselines among the games despite the pockets of blood and cannibalism, because alienation and unreality take more of the center stage, so it's good to see the Maw bring a bit of body horror to the table despite/because of the conceptual overlap with Werewolf's Gift of Hunger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-17T16:46:26-08:00","id":1531040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1530234-book-of-seemings-preview-q-a-coming-next-week?p=1531036#post1531036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The name is also extremely Soulsborne-y, upon reflection, which is apropos.<br /> <br /> <i>Visceral</i> is definitely the right word for what the Forgotten bring to the game; Changeling has one of the &quot;cleaner&quot; baselines among the games despite the pockets of blood and cannibalism, because alienation and unreality take more of the center stage, so it's good to see the Maw bring a bit of body horror to the table despite/because of the conceptual overlap with Werewolf's Gift of Hunger.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I can\u2019t take credit for the Trolls (I was on Stalker and Imp duty), one of my favourite things to write for Lost is monsters that remind you viscerally that this is a horror game. Working on the Forgotten definitely evoked the same feels that working on the Empty did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-18T03:27:48-08:00","id":1531053,"title":"","content":"All that this doing is making me want to become an Ogre main if/when I eventually get to play Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-18T12:09:12-08:00","id":1531065,"title":"","content":"Alright, I promised a look at the <b>Knockers</b>! I'm running behind schedule today, so no real commentary, but enjoy the excerpt, rate our book, join our Patreon, and have a great Sunday. I'll be back next time with the <b>Margrave of the Brim</b>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Knocker: A Tale of Deceit</b><br /> <br /> The most successful hunters aren\u2019t always the biggest or the fastest. Cleverness and patience can bring in prey at a much more reliable rate than wildly snapping at whatever crosses your path \u2014 just ask a Knocker. These would-be Wizened are the sharp-toothed gnomes and rhyme-talking spinners of fairytales, offering riches, knowledge, and magical favors to those they encounter, but always at a price. What they ask in return is simple, at first: a bowl of milk, some slivers of ash wood, maybe a few drops of blood\u2026<br /> <br /> Easy enough to lose, right? But as their victims become more reliant on favors, the price gets higher. And gorier.<br /> <br /> <b>Once</b><br /> <br /> Clever enough to escape but not quite clever enough to get home: That\u2019s the tragedy of the Knockers. Having slipped the Gentry\u2019s leash, they think themselves untouchable, too crafty to be caught again. Their arrogance is their downfall, for the Hedge loves to swallow up those who think they can\u2019t fail. Too late, Knockers discover that they\u2019ve only outsmarted themselves.<br /> <br /> When their minds are clear enough to hold a memory, Knockers endlessly replay their failed journeys, obsessing over every misstep, picking away at the thought of paths not taken, the choices that would have led them to a happier ending. This twisted regret breeds a resentful, spiteful creature who has nothing but hatred for the Lost. How is it fair that a lumbering Ogre made it home when a being of superior wit is trapped in the Thorns forever? This resentment fuels their attacks on changelings as much as their hunger for flesh does.<br /> <br /> Yet for all their bitterness, these Hungry Ones are social hunters. Lacking the brute strength or mystical allure of other Forgotten, Knockers trap their prey via more insidious methods, hooks baited with the keys to their desires.<br /> <br /> <b>Prey</b><br /> <br /> Knockers prey on the <b>desperate</b>. The smell of those who have a need so acute they\u2019ll do <i>anything</i> to fulfill it is delectable to these Forgotten. They often target those suffering from addiction and those who are in such dire straits that they\u2019ll make bargains with monsters in the dark. If a Knocker can\u2019t find his favorite prey, well, he\u2019ll <i>make</i> someone desperate \u2014 even if they\u2019re only desperate for the Knocker to stop their torment.<br /> <br /> <b>Lure</b><br /> <br /> A Knocker\u2019s Lure is <b>deals</b>, and they\u2019re rarely what they seem. They can conjure almost anything a victim desires, so long as they pay the agreed-upon price. These gifts are temporary but addictive, and those who continue to do business with a Knocker will eventually become so dependent they\u2019ll willingly agree to the creature\u2019s hardest sales pitches: first a finger or two, then a foot, then a neighbor. However, while they\u2019re usually relentless hagglers, a well-fed Knocker will sometimes offer fairer deals to those she encounters in an attempt to appease her own guilt and try to prove to herself she\u2019s not a total monster. Soon enough, though, the hunger comes clawing back and devours any notion she may have momentarily entertained about fair play or mercy.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing</b><br /> <br /> This blessing is similar to making a bargain (<b>Changeling</b>, p. 214), except as noted below:<br /> <br /> A Knocker can make a deal with changelings, hobgoblins, and humans.<ul><li>Making deals with a Knocker is addictive. The subject\u2019s player must make a successful Resolve + Composure roll every time he agrees to a deal. Failure means he gains the Addicted Condition for bargaining with the Hungry One.</li> <li>A Knocker can spend a Willpower to craft a talisman that can provide a benefit he wouldn\u2019t normally be able to give, but its power is temporary; it crumbled into bits of detritus after a number of weeks pass equal to the Hungry One\u2019s Wyrd (or sooner, if the Knocker wishes). However, the subject is always welcome to make another deal.</li> <li>Knockers don\u2019t gain mortal camouflage from this ability; they don\u2019t need it. Instead, the Hungry One always knows the location of anyone they have an ongoing deal with and the location of the Hedge gate nearest to that person.</li> <li>If a subject violates the deal, the consequences are always the same: They\u2019re drawn into the Hedge and deposited near the Knocker, who is always aware when this happens.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer